# Should I still be looking this often when comfortable?
#
# The whole cadence review, as data. Note what is NOT in it: soil, moisture, plants, or any
# number this file chose. The thresholds are the constitution's, the room is the reviewer's
# intersection of world and self, and the evidence is statistics computable without knowing
# what a property means — so the same six lines would serve a society allocating electricity.
#
# `$me`, `$evidence` and `$beliefs` are the three things a shipped rule cannot know and are
# substituted before it runs. Everything else is discovered. Prefixes come from store.PREFIXES,
# exactly as for a query in Python — a rule must not carry its own.
#
#   spread = 0        the instrument did not move AT ALL -> likelier broken than the world is
#                     still, so watch closer, not less
#   spread > steady   it is telling me something -> keep looking
#   otherwise         nothing is happening and unanimously so -> let the board sleep
#
# Relaxing needs every sensor to agree; tightening needs one dissenter. The cost of watching a
# still pot too closely is some battery; the cost of the reverse is a dead plant.
#
# See knowledge/decisions/a-belief-is-a-pick-within-a-range.md.

SELECT ?term ?value WHERE {
  { SELECT (MIN(?s) AS ?lo) (MAX(?s) AS ?hi) (MIN(?n) AS ?least) WHERE {
      GRAPH <$evidence> { ?e a ag:Evidence ; ag:sampleSpread ?s ; ag:sampleCount ?n } } }
  GRAPH ?o { ag:PerceptionCapability ag:steadyFraction ?steady ; ag:reviewWindow ?window }
  GRAPH <$evidence> { ?r a ag:Range ; ag:onTerm ag:slowSleepS ;
                         ag:notBelow ?floor ; ag:notAbove ?ceiling }
  FILTER(?least >= ?window)
  BIND(ag:slowSleepS AS ?term)
  BIND(IF(?lo = 0.0 || ?hi > ?steady, ?floor, ?ceiling) AS ?value)
}
